&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Atlantic seeks a highly motivated Annuity Director to join our distribution team in a client-facing, externally focused role serving the Independent Marketing Organization (IMO) channel. This team-based position works collaboratively with National Accounts and Internal Sales Support to represent Global Atlantic&#39;s strategies and solutions to IMO partners and their sales forces (marketers). The Annuity Director serves as a strategic liaison between Global Atlantic and distribution partners, responsible for driving sales growth, deepening relationships, and ensuring effective communication and execution of our value proposition in the marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TEAM STRUCTURE &amp;amp; COLLABORATION&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Annuity Director operates within a collaborative team environment consisting of:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;National Accounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners closely with SVP National Accounts and Strategic Partnerships to develop and execute account-based business strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aligns on territory priorities, account segmentation, and strategic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinates on key account planning and relationship escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Internal Sales Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates with internal wholesalers to develop new and established relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages internal resources for proposal development, product expertise, and client servicing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures seamless coordination between field activities and home office support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team-based approach ensures strategic alignment, operational efficiency, and a unified client experience across all touchpoints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CORE RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;External Relationship Management &amp;amp; Client Engagement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Primary Accountability: Serve as the face of Global Atlantic to IMO partners and their sales forces, delivering strategies and solutions that drive business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong, productive, and profitable relationships with assigned IMO distribution partners to capture market share and exceed sales goals in the annuity channel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage client relationships primarily through face-to-face engagement, supplemented by telephone and email communications, ensuring consistent presence and accessibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Global Atlantic&#39;s strategies, products, and solutions to IMO leadership and their sales forces (marketers), positioning our value proposition effectively in competitive situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver presentations and communicate the Global Atlantic story with clarity, consistency, and impact to diverse audiences including IMO executives, sales leaders, and field marketers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategic Execution &amp;amp; Sales Performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet and exceed annuity sales goals for assigned accounts through disciplined territory management and relationship development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute account-based business strategies in partnership with National Accounts leadership, ensuring alignment between corporate objectives and field execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep understanding of the competitive landscape within the insurance industry, using market intelligence to inform strategy and positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain features, benefits, and advantages of Global Atlantic products to clients with precision and persuasive impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Accountability&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize deliberate scheduling and calendar management to maximize client time and ensure activities correspond to territory priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Salesforce account information and content for all assigned accounts, maintaining data integrity and documentation standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage individual expenses and budget in accordance with company guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take personal accountability for the execution of goals and objectives, consistently meeting or exceeding performance expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KEY COMPETENCIES &amp;amp; QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of sales experience in the annuity and life insurance industry, preferably in the IMO annuity channel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in wholesaling and relationship management with proven ability to drive and increase sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and influencing skills with the ability to deliver information articulately and consistently to external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship management capabilities, including the ability to build trust, navigate complex organizational structures, and influence decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking and execution orientation, balancing long-term relationship development with short-term sales objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset with ability to work effectively across internal teams and leverage resources to serve clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to quickly learn product lines, procedures, and workflows in a dynamic business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in expense management, negotiation, and professional communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Licensing &amp;amp; Travel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 7, 63, and Life &amp;amp; Health licenses (or ability to obtain quickly)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant travel required – successful candidates may work remotely but must be willing to travel extensively to meet client needs and territory demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SUCCESS METRICS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Performance in this role will be evaluated based on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales Results: Achievement of annuity sales goals and market share growth in assigned accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship Depth: Quality and breadth of relationships with IMO partners and their sales forces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Alignment: Effectiveness in executing account-based strategies in partnership with National Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client Satisfaction: Feedback from IMO partners regarding responsiveness, value delivery, and partnership quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Collaboration: Contribution to team objectives and effective utilization of Internal Sales Support resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Intelligence: Quality of competitive insights and ability to position Global Atlantic effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ROLE DISTINCTION&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Annuity Director position is distinguished by its:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External, client-facing focus with primary accountability for IMO partner relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-based operating model requiring close collaboration with National Accounts and Internal Sales Support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic communication responsibility as the voice of Global Atlantic to distribution partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dual accountability for both relationship management and sales performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field-based execution with significant autonomy and travel requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Annuity Director serves as a critical link between Global Atlantic&#39;s corporate strategy and marketplace execution, ensuring our solutions reach advisors and clients through strong, strategically aligned IMO partnerships&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary for this position is $75,000 plus monthly variable incentive compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR will provide reasonable accommodations as required by applicable federal, state, and/or local laws. Individuals seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process should email&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Emails sent for unrelated issues, such as following up on an application, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kkr.com/careers&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.kkr.com/careers&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1774021690220000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1AG2WRszai8PfCsE-FH5EJ&quot;&gt;https://www.kkr.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;because of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Only emails left for this purpose will be returned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. This notice&amp;nbsp;applies only&amp;nbsp;to applicants and employees who work or will work in Massachusetts, in accordance with applicable state law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Annuity Specialist Processor is responsible for the accurate and timely processing of post-issue annuity transactions while delivering exceptional service to internal and external customers. This role reviews, researches, and completes a variety of policy servicing requests, financial adjustments, and transaction corrections in accordance with company policies, regulatory requirements, and service level expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is detail-oriented, analytical, and thrives in a fast-paced environment. This position requires strong problem-solving skills, the ability to manage multiple priorities, and collaboration across Operations, Customer Service, Compliance, Finance, and other business partners to resolve complex servicing requests and improve operational efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process a wide variety of post-issue annuity transactions, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Policy updates and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payment corrections and reversals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check reissues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other policy servicing requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and resolve complex policy inquiries, discrepancies, and escalated servicing issues accurately and within established service standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review transactions for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with internal controls, regulatory requirements, and company guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain detailed documentation of policy administration activities within the policy administration system and supporting applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Service, Operations, Finance, Compliance, Legal, and other business units to resolve exceptions and ensure positive customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze servicing processes and recommend improvements that increase efficiency, accuracy, and customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with testing, implementation, and ongoing support of process enhancements and system improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in special projects and departmental initiatives that support operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized, audit-ready records and ensure adherence to quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
