&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR seeks to recruit an Assistant Vice President overseeing the Investment Operations teams that support KKR Insurance’s $80B real estate portfolio, which includes commercial mortgages, residential mortgages, commercial real estate equity, and residential equity. The ideal candidate will excel at multi-tasking under pressure with minimal supervision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Sr. analysts and analysts responsible for asset set up for new securities and structured transactions – coordinate with Portfolio Management team to (ii) understand new structures and (ii) build-out infrastructure to support new structures in KKR’s Investment Management Platforms (LMS, Geneva, etc)
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up SPVs to hold assets and facilitate internal securitization of asset cashflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive of settlement of loans/assets, onward participation of loans/assets across KKR Portfolios – coordination with Legal and custody banks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Sr. analysts and analysts responsible for funding and settlement of all deal flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Sr. analysts and analysts responsible for ongoing asset lifecycle management (Principal and Interest Remittances, Pay-downs, Pay-offs, coupon updates, factor updates, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review cash and asset movement across KKR custody and trust banks and accounts related to Investment Activity (trades, transfers, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface and manage the relationship with third party servicers (loan servicers, asset managers, Federal Home Loan Banks, Custodian Banks, etc.) &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate above activities with Investment Accounting, Investment Controls, Risk, Asset Allocation, Investment Origination , etc. &amp;nbsp;– inclusive of interfaces with ancillary platforms/systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify processes enhancements and develop an implementation program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervision, train, and mentor direct FTEs supporting the above&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6-10 years&#39; experience in general investment operations, ideally in a middle office or other transaction-facing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in private credit or equity deal funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of credit investments, particularly bank loans or real estate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multi-task, and oversee a high volume of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong work ethic with the ability to quickly grasp key concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
