&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION OVERVIEW&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Reinsurance Management position will act as the key contact for internal and external queries related to reinsurance on both Life and Annuity products. Additionally, this role will be the primary point of contact for reinsurers and reinsurance administrator TAI. &amp;nbsp;This position will coordinate and interact internally including product development, corporate actuarial, legal and IT. External interactions include our third party reinsurance partners, external reinsurers and key stakeholders. Position is being considered to join our Des Moines office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze financial impact of changes in reinsurance coverage and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversight of work effort performed by the reinsurance TPA and internal modeling team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and present to internal committees and senior management ongoing program performance and potential strategic management decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people skills, including external relationship management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide product and system expertise related to reinsurance for all areas of the company and our reinsurance third party administrator (TPA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to escalated issues relating to reinsurance pricing, implementation or queries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to reinsurance and/or actuarial background required. Approx. (3-5) years of financial services industry experience is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with life and annuity product features is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A “go getter” mentality, taking initiative and suggesting a course of action independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to present technical information to non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
