&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Global Atlantic is seeking an Assistant Vice President to join its Treasury &amp;amp; Capital Markets team in the Boston office. This person will own the operational management of the firm’s Funding Agreement and FABN programs end-to-end — from issuance through repayment. The role requires close coordination across many internal teams, leadership of the Quarterly FABN Program Update cycle, and serving as a day-to-day point of contact for the funding agreement business.&amp;nbsp; Periodic travel to the New York office will be expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full lifecycle of Funding Agreement and FABN deals, including live deal execution, settlement coordination, interest payments, principal repayments, and maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all deal documentation workflows — distribution notes, ratings agency letters, regulatory filings, and signature packets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deal tracking files, payment schedules, interest accruals, and expense documentation across all active issuances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deal tracking files, payment schedules, interest accruals, and expense documentation across all active issuances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Quarterly FABN Program Update end-to-end: due diligence, MD&amp;amp;A disclosure review, legal alignment, auditor coordination, exchange filings, and final signatures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate across Legal, Statutory Reporting, external auditors, and outside counsel to keep quarterly deliverables on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary operational coordinator across Treasury Operations, Investment Operations, Finance, and Legal on all FA/FABN workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage expense tracking and reinsurance cost coordination, ensuring accurate documentation and timely communication downstream.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Treasury &amp;amp; Capital Markets function in the Boston office, serving as the local point of contact for the broader funding agreement business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for process improvement and contribute to automation and technology initiatives across the FA/FABN platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI-powered tools to improve productivity and quality of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about and openness to adopting emerging AI technologies in day-to-day workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy and relevance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree in finance, economics, accounting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8 years of professional experience with a track record of owning and improving operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast starter who takes initiative, thrives on managing complex processes, and proactively finds ways to make them better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail in high-volume, multi-workstream environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coordination and communication skills across multiple internal teams and external counterparties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead multi-stakeholder processes independently and drive workstreams to completion on tight timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of financial concepts; exposure to fixed income or capital markets is a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter comfortable operating with a high degree of independence in a satellite office setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
