&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KKR’s Gurugram&lt;/strong&gt; office provides best-in-class business operations services and solutions to our internal stakeholders and clients, drives organization-wide process efficiency and transformation, and reflects KKR&#39;s global culture and values of teamwork and innovation. The office contains multifunctional business capabilities and is integral in furthering the growth and transformation of KKR. The office was established with an initial concentration of finance, operations, and technology personnel, followed by the expansion of additional functions and capabilities. KKR’s creation of a Gurugram office builds upon the firm&#39;s momentum in India and bolsters its existing presence in Mumbai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEAM OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Finance supports the strategic direction of the Firm by ensuring effective financial planning, analysis, reporting, compliance, accounting, and stewardship of financial risks and controls. The Private Markets Valuation team is responsible for governance and oversight of the month and quarterly valuation process across private market investments, including the review of valuation methodologies, key assumptions, supporting analyses, and related reporting.&lt;br&gt;The team partners with investment professionals, Fund Controllership, external valuation specialists, auditors, Tax, Legal, Technology, Client Services, and other stakeholders to support consistent, well-controlled, and timely fair value conclusions. It also develops valuation analytics and reporting used by senior management, valuation committees, investors, and other internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Principal role responsible for leading key elements of the private market’s valuation process from Gurugram. The individual will provide senior review and challenge of valuation analyses, oversee the quality and timeliness of team deliverables, manage and develop local team members, and serve as a senior partner to the global Valuation team and other stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;The role requires strong valuation judgment, financial and accounting acumen, leadership capability, and the ability to manage complex cross-functional processes. The Principal will also help advance the Valuation team operating model through stronger data, reporting, controls, automation, and use of AI-enabled tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLES &amp;amp; RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Lead and oversee key components of the valuation process across KKR private markets portfolios, ensuring deliverables are accurate, complete, timely, and consistent with established policies and procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Review and challenge valuation models, memoranda, and supporting analyses prepared by investment teams and valuation professionals across a range of asset classes and valuation methodologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Evaluate key valuation assumptions, including financial forecasts, comparable company and transaction multiples, discount rates, capital structures, leverage, net debt, exit assumptions, liquidity considerations, and other company-specific adjustments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Assess period-over-period movements in fair value, realized and unrealized performance, cash flows, cost, ownership, and other key investment metrics; investigate and resolve unexplained or inconsistent movements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Provide senior-level review of valuation reporting, performance schedules, cash flow reporting, and related materials used by Finance, Client Services, Product Management, senior management, and other stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Coordinate with global Valuation team members, investment teams, Fund Controllership, external valuation specialists, and auditors to manage valuation timelines, open items, review comments, and escalation matters.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Support the preparation and review of materials for asset-level Valuation Committees, Global Valuation Committees, Audit Committee reporting, and other governance forums.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Identify valuation, reporting, data, and control risks and ensure issues are appropriately documented, escalated, remediated, and incorporated into future processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Interpret and apply relevant fair value accounting guidance, valuation policies, and internal governance standards, including US GAAP fair value principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Manage, coach, and develop Gurugram-based valuation professionals; establish clear responsibilities, review standards, performance expectations, and training plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Allocate work across the local team and oversee execution during peak reporting periods, balancing deadlines, complexity, development opportunities, and quality requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Build strong working relationships with global stakeholders and operate as a senior extension of the Valuation leadership team in Gurugram.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Develop and maintain portfolio-level valuation analytics, dashboards, management reporting, and exception-based review tools across metrics such as MOIC, valuation methodology, discount rates, leverage, and valuation movements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Oversee data management and reconciliations supporting the valuation process, including alignment among valuation systems, fund accounting records, cash flow data, ownership information, and reporting outputs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Partner with Technology, Data Operations, and Finance teams on enhancements to valuation systems, reporting infrastructure, data-lake solutions, workflow tools, and control frameworks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Drive process simplification, standardization, and automation initiatives that improve efficiency, scalability, transparency, and audit readiness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Identify appropriate opportunities to use generative AI and other automation tools in valuation review, data extraction, reconciliation, analytics, and knowledge management while maintaining effective human review and control.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Support responses to external audit, internal audit, regulatory, investor, and other diligence requests relating to valuation processes, methodologies, controls, and reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Contribute to valuation policy, procedure, governance, and control enhancements, including implementation of new requirements and communication of expectations to stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Prepare and review ad hoc valuation analyses and reports for senior management and other stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;15+ years of relevant experience in private markets valuation, transaction advisory, investment banking, private equity finance, valuation consulting, audit, or a comparable financial services environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;CA qualification required; CFA, CPA, MBA, or other relevant advanced qualification preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong knowledge of private markets valuation techniques, including discounted cash flow, comparable company, precedent transaction, and other income- and market-based approaches.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong understanding of financial statements, capital structures, investment performance, cash flows, and fair value accounting principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Demonstrated ability to review complex valuation analyses, exercise sound judgment, identify inconsistencies, and communicate conclusions clearly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Prior experience leading teams and reviewing the work of junior and mid-level professionals, with a strong commitment to coaching and development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Exceptionally strong financial, analytical, and problem-solving capabilities, with the ability to work with complex datasets while maintaining a high degree of accuracy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong business acumen and the ability to quickly understand complex businesses, investment structures, operating models, and valuation considerations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Excellent organizational and project management skills, with the ability to prioritize, multitask, and deliver under tight deadlines with limited direction.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong interpersonal and collaboration skills, with the ability to build credibility and partner effectively across investment teams, Finance, Technology, Operations, Tax, Legal, and external advisers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex valuation matters to senior and non-technical audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong risk and control mindset, with the ability to identify, assess, escalate, and mitigate potential valuation and reporting risks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Advanced Microsoft Office skills, particularly Excel, PowerPoint, and Word; experience with Power BI, valuation platforms, Investran, or other financial systems is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Professional demeanor, sound judgment, high ethical standards, and comfort handling sensitive and confidential information.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Intellectual curiosity, ownership mentality, and comfort operating in an evolving, high-growth, and globally integrated environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Highly organized self-starter who can operate independently while remaining committed to teamwork and the broader success of the Firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience valuing investments across one or more private markets asset classes, such as private equity, infrastructure, real estate, growth equity, or private credit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience working with third-party valuation firms, external auditors, or formal valuation committee processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Comfort using AI-powered tools to improve the efficiency and quality of work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy, completeness, and relevance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience identifying and implementing opportunities to apply AI, automation, data visualization, or workflow tools to improve business processes and outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR will provide reasonable accommodations as required by applicable federal, state, and/or local laws. Individuals seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process should email&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Emails sent for unrelated issues, such as following up on an application, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kkr.com/careers&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.kkr.com/careers&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1774021690220000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1AG2WRszai8PfCsE-FH5EJ&quot;&gt;https://www.kkr.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;because of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Only emails left for this purpose will be returned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. This notice&amp;nbsp;applies only&amp;nbsp;to applicants and employees who work or will work in Massachusetts, in accordance with applicable state law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR&#39;s Gurugram office provides best-in-class business operations services and solutions to our internal stakeholders and clients, drives organization-wide process efficiency and transformation, and reflects KKR&#39;s global culture and values of teamwork and innovation. The office contains multifunctional business capabilities and is integral in furthering the growth and transformation of KKR. The office was established with an initial concentration of finance, operations, and technology personnel, followed by the expansion of additional functions and capabilities. KKR’s creation of a Gurugram office builds upon the firm&#39;s momentum in India and bolsters its existing presence in Mumbai.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEAM OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The&amp;nbsp;EMEA&amp;nbsp;Regional&amp;nbsp;Finance&amp;nbsp;Team serves as the strategic and operational finance partner for KKR’s offices and operating entities across EMEA. Our team supports regional leadership by managing budgets and forecasts which helps drive strategic decision making with valuable financial insights, provide regional entity governance and oversight of statutory, regulatory &amp;amp; tax requirements and implement and maintain systems to ensure accuracy of financial data, processes &amp;amp; controls. Working closely with the wider KKR organization and global Finance team, we also contribute to firmwide initiatives by incorporating regional requirements and supporting business development efforts as needed.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR&#39;s EMEA Finance team is seeking a highly motivated, commercially minded and detail-oriented finance professional to join its Finance team based in Gurugram. This role will support the EMEA Finance function, partnering closely with the London and Gurugram Finance team, global FP&amp;amp;A colleagues in the US and local EMEA leadership and deal teams. The success candidate will be responsible for preparing, reviewing and enhancing key finance deliverables in the following areas:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLES &amp;amp; RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Management Reporting &amp;amp; Business Partnering&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the production of quarterly consolidated EMEA management reporting packs, including P&amp;amp;L analysis, business line reporting,&amp;nbsp;AuM,&amp;nbsp;monetization’s&amp;nbsp;and Deployments and other&amp;nbsp;key metrics&amp;nbsp;and additional management analytics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparation and review of OPEX reporting, including coordination with offshore support teams and local finance stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare quarterly reporting for strategy heads, presenting key performance metrics and revenue variances by deal and fund, with clear commentary on drivers of performance against budget and prior periods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the preparation of EMEA annual budgets, quarterly forecasts and long-range financial models across business lines, profit&amp;nbsp;centres, cost&amp;nbsp;centres&amp;nbsp;and legal entities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review detailed variance analysis across revenues, expenses, deployment and&amp;nbsp;monetization’s, allocations and other key financial metrics, providing clear commentary on drivers, trends, risks and opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the&amp;nbsp;EMEA&amp;nbsp;forecasting process by preparing accurate financial&amp;nbsp;inputs, analysis and commentary for submission to senior&amp;nbsp;EMEA&amp;nbsp;leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering&amp;nbsp;with the&amp;nbsp;deal teams,&amp;nbsp;London Finance&amp;nbsp;and central FPA&amp;nbsp;teams&amp;nbsp;in order to&amp;nbsp;provide timely and accurate analytics to support business decision-making by regional senior management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly and quarterly&amp;nbsp;Board Packs on legal entity financial&amp;nbsp;management information packs for senior stakeholders, including expense analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the EMEA CFO with ad hoc analysis, regional finance priorities, cost management initiatives and strategic projects requiring strong financial judgement and cross-functional coordination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, monitor and report&amp;nbsp;to Business heads&amp;nbsp;on expenses, cost allocations and business performance metrics to support cost management and financial discipline across the region.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop dashboards, analytical models and reporting templates to improve visibility of expenses, KPIs, trends and business performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;Financial Accounting&amp;nbsp;&amp;amp; Audits&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and support month-end and year-end close processes, under both local GAAP and IFRS accounting standards, across&amp;nbsp;several&amp;nbsp;management companies&amp;nbsp;inclusive of posting and reviewing journals,&amp;nbsp;performing and documenting key profit and loss and balance sheet reconciliations, IFRS 2 share-based payment accounting charges,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;revenue recognition activities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining&amp;nbsp;strong internal controls&amp;nbsp;and documentation&amp;nbsp;relating&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;these&amp;nbsp;financial accounting processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconciliations between KKR’s ledgers and those of its local service providers for certain EMEA management companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Gurugram and London Finance team to fulfil regulatory filing obligations, Finance Board pack report and audits where required&amp;nbsp;for EMEA management companies.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare Financial statements under local jurisdictional languages and in compliance with local GAAP and IFRS accounting standards under Corporate and consolidated structures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deliverables to the UK finance team and various external audit teams across EMEA relating to interim and annual statutory audits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address internal audit queries and support the implementation of audit recommendations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare Supporting Accounting Memos for external auditors and Shareholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arrange the appropriate documentation required for financial statements to be signed and filed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Project Management, Systems, Data &amp;amp; Process Improvement&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design, enhancement and automation of Finance reporting processes using tools such as Excel, Power BI, SAP Analytics Cloud, OneStream or similar reporting platforms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline manual reporting, improve data quality, reduce process inefficiencies and strengthen controls.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the EMEA CFO and senior Finance leadership with the project management of regional and global Finance initiatives, including reporting enhancements, systems implementation, process redesign and operating model improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent work experience required&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified chartered accountant with&amp;nbsp;~5 years post-qualified experience;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience in FP&amp;amp;A, management reporting, financial control, corporate finance or business finance, ideally within financial services, asset management, private equity, investment banking or a large global corporate environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing senior management packs, executive-level financial analysis, KPI reporting and clear commentary for senior stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;Strong PowerPoint and presentation skills, with the ability to convert financial analysis into concise, executive-ready materials.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in entity controllership consisting of ownership of month-end and year-end close – journal entries, accruals, prepayments, balance sheet reconciliations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Statutory accounts preparation and audit support (liaising with external auditors and managing PBC lists)&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in tax compliance coordination (VAT, corporation tax filings, withholding tax)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work with external service providers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret complex financial data and communicate insights clearly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and a focus on accuracy, completeness, documentation and review discipline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel capability, including complex formulas, pivot tables, lookups, data tables, scenario modelling, structured templates and large dataset manipulation.&amp;nbsp;Inclusive of&amp;nbsp;practical experience using Excel to automate,&amp;nbsp;standardize&amp;nbsp;and improve finance processes, including Power Query, Power Pivot, VBA/macros, dynamic arrays, advanced charting and model audit controls.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with business intelligence and reporting tools such as Power BI, SAP Analytics Cloud, OneStream or comparable ERP/EPM/reporting platforms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly&amp;nbsp;organized&amp;nbsp;and able to manage multiple deliverables, deadlines and stakeholder requests across recurring reporting cycles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player with the ability to work across geographies and manage&amp;nbsp;inputs&amp;nbsp;from local, offshore and global teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, including the ability to challenge constructively, explain financial results clearly and escalate issues appropriately.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates professionalism, integrity and sound judgement when handling sensitive financial information.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, innovative and willing to take ownership of process improvements while maintaining strong execution discipline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI-powered tools to improve productivity and quality of work&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about and openness to adopting emerging AI technologies in day-to-day workflows&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy and relevance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
