&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEAM OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Atlantic is a Top 3 preneed life insurance provider, distributing primarily through approximately 2,400 funeral homes, third-party organizations, and national accounts across the U.S. The Preneed Business Development &amp;amp; Strategic Accounts team is responsible for growing profitable production through our largest and most strategically important distribution partners — including national firms, third-party marketing organizations, and select independent accounts — while continuing to prospect and onboard new relationships in line with the division&#39;s growth plan.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Principal, Business Development &lt;/span&gt;is a senior individual-contributor role responsible for driving profitable growth across an assigned book of strategic preneed distribution partners and for opening new national and multi-location accounts. Reporting to preneed sales leadership, the Principal owns the end-to-end account strategy — from prospecting and pitching, through contracting and onboarding, to ongoing production management, joint business planning, and executive relationship stewardship. The role partners closely with Regional Sales team, marketing, product, operations, legal, and compliance to translate distributor needs into commercial outcomes and to ensure Global Atlantic remains the carrier of choice in the preneed market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own an assigned portfolio of strategic accounts (national firms, third-party organizations, and select independent partners); develop and execute account-level business plans that meet or exceed annual preneed sales, retention, and profitability targets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect, qualify, and close new strategic account relationships, leading contracting, onboarding, and go-live in coordination with sales leadership, legal, compliance, and operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the senior day-to-day relationship owner for principals, corporate leaders, and top-producing agents at assigned firms; conduct regular business reviews, joint planning sessions, and on-site visits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Regional Sales, Account Management and Strategic Accounts team to translate pipeline activity into closed production, ensuring accounts receive best-in-class sales support and product positioning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the distributor internally — surfacing product, illustration, technology, and service enhancements to product, marketing, and operations, and shaping the roadmap for strategic accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive-level presentations, RFP responses, and industry-conference engagement (e.g., ICCFA, NFDA, state association meetings) to build Global Atlantic&#39;s brand and pipeline in the preneed community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain rigorous CRM discipline in Salesforce — logging activity, forecasting production, and providing accurate weekly and monthly pipeline reporting to preneed leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and informally mentor Senior Analysts, Sales Consultants, and other members of the strategic accounts team; model KKR / Global Atlantic values in every internal and external interaction.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience; 8+ years of progressive sales, business development, or key/strategic account management experience, with meaningful time in life insurance, annuities, or preneed distribution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of carrying and exceeding a multi-million-dollar production or premium quota through third-party distribution (funeral homes, IMOs, TPMs, or national accounts strongly preferred).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to open, contract, and scale complex, multi-stakeholder distribution relationships from prospect to top-producing account.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of preneed and/or life insurance product mechanics, illustrations, and regulatory considerations across multiple states; ability to explain features, benefits, and competitive positioning to sophisticated audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive presence with credibility to advise principals and C-suite counterparts at large funeral service operators and marketing organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in Salesforce and modern sales technologies; disciplined about pipeline hygiene, activity metrics, and data-driven account planning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life insurance licensing (or willingness to obtain within a defined onboarding period) as required by role and jurisdictions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel 8–12 nights per month across the U.S.; this is a remote role working from a home office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRITICAL COMPETENCIES FOR SUCCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Account Ownership – thinks like a general manager of the account, balancing near-term production with multi-year relationship equity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consultative Selling &amp;amp; Executive Presence – earns trust with sophisticated distributors and closes complex, multi-stakeholder deals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preneed / Life Insurance Acumen – deep working knowledge of preneed products, distribution economics, and the funeral services ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pipeline &amp;amp; Forecasting Discipline – rigorous CRM, activity, and forecasting habits; predictable delivery against plan.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration – partners effectively with Sales Desk, product, marketing, operations, legal, and compliance to remove friction for distributors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results Orientation &amp;amp; Ownership – takes personal accountability for account outcomes; resilient in a quota-carrying environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Influence – clear, polished written and verbal communication across agents, principals, and internal executives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity &amp;amp; Regulatory Awareness – operates with a high compliance bar in a regulated, multi-state insurance environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR will provide reasonable accommodations as required by applicable federal, state, and/or local laws. Individuals seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process should email&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Emails sent for unrelated issues, such as following up on an application, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kkr.com/careers&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.kkr.com/careers&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1774021690220000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1AG2WRszai8PfCsE-FH5EJ&quot;&gt;https://www.kkr.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;because of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Only emails left for this purpose will be returned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. This notice&amp;nbsp;applies only&amp;nbsp;to applicants and employees who work or will work in Massachusetts, in accordance with applicable state law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEAM OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR’s Corporate Communications team is responsible for internal and external communications globally, management of KKR’s corporate narrative, and serving as spokespeople for the firm. The team supports the firm with overall messaging, transaction work, portfolio company support, media relations, employee engagement, executive communications, and crafting a variety of related content and thought leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is seeking a seasoned financial communications professional to join its Global Communications team with a primary focus on the firm’s insurance platform and broader credit-oriented businesses. Reporting to senior communications leadership, this individual will own the communications strategy for one of the fastest-growing areas of the firm—spanning life, retirement, and reinsurance under the Global Atlantic brand—while also serving as a key contributor to corporate communications priorities across the U.S. market. The ideal candidate brings deep fluency in financial services, insurance and credit markets, established relationships with top-tier financial media, and the judgment to operate with autonomy in a fast-moving, high-stakes environment. This role is based in KKR’s New York office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the development and execution of integrated communications strategies for the firm’s global insurance platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted communications advisor to senior investment and business leaders, translating complex insurance and credit market dynamics into clear, compelling narratives for external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive proactive and reactive media relations—cultivating relationships with key financial, insurance, and trade journalists; developing messaging; and managing press engagement around transactions, earnings, and strategic milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive communications efforts including thought leadership, speaking platforms, bylined articles, and high-profile announcements for senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with communications colleagues across regions to ensure consistency of messaging and alignment on cross-platform and cross-border initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to broader global corporate communications priorities, including high-stakes projects, emerging issues, and firm-wide campaigns as they arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the insurance, credit, and broader financial services competitive landscape to identify communications opportunities and inform positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a central role in crisis communications and reputational risk management, providing counsel and rapid-response support when situations arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–15 years of progressive experience in financial communications, with a portion spent in or around the insurance, reinsurance, or credit markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in insurance-sector communications, including familiarity with regulatory dynamics, ratings agency processes, and the financial fundamentals of life, annuity, or reinsurance businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of private credit and broader private markets (e.g., private equity, real assets, leveraged finance); experience at an alternative asset manager, investment bank, insurer, or top-tier financial communications agency strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with financial and insurance trade media; demonstrated track record of securing high-quality coverage and managing sensitive press situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree in business, finance, or communications a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRITICAL COMPETENCIES FOR SUCCESS &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset—ability to see around corners, anticipate issues, and develop communications plans that advance business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing, editing, and message-development skills with the ability to distill complex financial and insurance concepts for diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep financial literacy—comfortable interpreting earnings, credit ratings, capital structures, and regulatory developments and translating them into communications strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence and the confidence to advise, influence, and collaborate with senior leaders across investment, legal, and business teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship builder who instinctively cultivates networks—across newsrooms, industry forums, and internal stakeholder groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a high-tempo, entrepreneurial environment; able to manage multiple workstreams simultaneously with sound judgment and minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous attention to detail and a versatile content skill set—from talking points and press materials to thought leadership, presentations, and digital content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and low-ego; genuinely enjoys partnering across teams and geographies to deliver outstanding results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI-powered tools to improve productivity and quality of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about and openness to adopting emerging AI technologies in day-to-day workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy and relevance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-ONSITE&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;This is the expected annual base salary range for this New York-based position. Actual salaries may vary based on factors, such as skill, experience, and qualification for the role. Employees may be eligible for a discretionary bonus, based on factors such as individual and team performance.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
