&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR&#39;s Gurugram office provides best in class services and solutions to our internal stakeholders and clients, drives organization wide process efficiency and transformation, and reflects KKR&#39;s global culture and values of teamwork and innovation. The office contains multifunctional business capabilities and is integral in furthering the growth and transformation of KKR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;KKR’s Global Human Capital (“HC”) team provides commercially aligned people strategies by working closely with business leaders, employees, and key stakeholders to deliver on human capital and talent needs. The HC team accomplishes this by implementing world class, advisory &amp;amp; talent solutions that:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive first quartile investment performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create differentiated outcomes aligned with the firm’s strategic priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide an exceptional employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preserve (and evolve) our unique culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and analytics to inform our decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect the firm’s license to operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;KKR’s Human Capital team is comprised of Business Partners &amp;amp; Centres of Excellence (Talent Development, Talent Acquisition, People Ops &amp;amp; Data, Culture, Total Rewards, etc...). Together, they seamlessly deliver human capital services and solutions, across all stages of an employee’s lifecycle at KKR.&lt;br&gt;The Talent Acquisition (“TA”) team within Human Capital was launched in 2020 with a small, US focused effort. Today, we are a global team of 20+ with capabilities to recruit from campus and other early career pipelines through to senior, experienced hires across our Asset Management, Insurance and Business Operations groups. We are now focused on growing our APAC TA platform and the team is committed to building strong partnerships across the firm, and is a tight-knit, collaborative group that values excellence and teamwork.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;KKR is seeking a dynamic and experienced recruiter to join the firm’s growing APAC Talent Acquisition team and support our Business Operations recruiting efforts based in Gurugram. This is a contractual role for a period of one year, engaged through a third-party payroll. This individual will play an integral role in shaping the firm’s talent strategy by helping to identify, attract, and engage top-tier candidates in support of KKR’s continued global growth.&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate will have a broad range of non-tech recruiting experience in the financial services industry across corporate functions such as finance, legal, operations, human capital, and other business support areas. They will be able to operate independently and drive full-cycle recruiting efforts from end to end in a fast-paced, high-volume environment. The ideal candidate is highly organized, self-motivated, collaborative, and resilient, with a keen eye for both strategic alignment and detail execution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Responsibilities&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Manage full-cycle recruitment for non-tech roles across Finance, Legal, Operations, Human Capital, and other corporate/business support functions.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Act as a trusted advisor to hiring managers — providing guidance on hiring strategy, market insights, and process best practices from the market.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Build and maintain strong talent pipelines through multiple sourcing channels (direct sourcing, referrals, market mapping, etc.).&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Evaluate, interview, and present high-caliber candidates, ensuring thoughtful feedback loops and continuous refinement of search strategy.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Partner closely with senior business leaders and Human Capital Business Partners to anticipate demand and proactively build talent pipelines.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Bring forward innovative sourcing approaches and ideas to enhance efficiency and candidate quality.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Participate actively in hiring manager discussions to stay aligned with business changes and talent priorities; act as a subject matter expert for non-tech recruitment.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ensure an exceptional candidate experience — maintaining timely communication, sharing feedback, and representing the firm’s values throughout the process.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Educate candidates on the firm’s culture, growth opportunities, and value proposition.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Lead compensation and offer discussions with both hiring managers and candidates to ensure competitive, informed, and timely closures.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Leverage Greenhouse to its full functionality for requisition management, pipeline tracking, and data integrity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;5–8 years of proven experience in non-tech recruitment within a high-performing corporate or search firm environment (preferably financial services).&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong understanding of non-tech corporate function roles, evolving skillsets, and market trends across finance, controls, operations, and business support.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Demonstrated ability to engage and influence senior stakeholders.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience hiring across multiple disciplines and managing competing priorities with agility.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong business acumen and ability to translate business needs into talent strategies.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Excellent interpersonal and communication skills; comfortable interacting with senior candidates and business leaders.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Creative, results-oriented, and adaptable to change.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Proven ability to manage confidential information with discretion.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Expertise in direct sourcing and in engaging passive candidates.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience managing complex compensation and offer negotiations.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Proficiency in using Applicant Tracking Systems (Greenhouse preferred).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement &amp;amp; Work Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;This is a contractual position for a duration of one year, engaged and paid through a third-party payroll provider.&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;KKR operates a hybrid work structure, with 4 days per week working from the office (Gurugram).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR will provide reasonable accommodations as required by applicable federal, state, and/or local laws. Individuals seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process should email&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Emails sent for unrelated issues, such as following up on an application, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kkr.com/careers&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.kkr.com/careers&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1774021690220000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1AG2WRszai8PfCsE-FH5EJ&quot;&gt;https://www.kkr.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;because of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@kkr.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@kkr.com&lt;/a&gt;. Only emails left for this purpose will be returned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. This notice&amp;nbsp;applies only&amp;nbsp;to applicants and employees who work or will work in Massachusetts, in accordance with applicable state law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEAM OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will join the KKR Global Tax team, a world-class team of tax professionals dedicated to supporting KKR’s global investment activities. Led by the Global Head of Tax based out of New York, the team encompasses experts in various areas of taxation, including transaction structuring, compliance, and strategic planning. With a global presence and a focus on collaboration, KKR Global Tax plays a pivotal role in guiding the firm’s tax strategy and ensuring compliance with tax regulations across jurisdictions. The team fosters a culture of innovation, excellence, and continuous learning, providing opportunities for professional growth and development. As part of KKR Global Tax, the Insurance Tax Structuring role will have the opportunity to work alongside industry-leading professionals and contribute to the success of one of the world’s premier investment firms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is seeking a skilled and experienced tax professional to join its tax team in Boston, with a focus on insurance tax matters for Global Atlantic and KKR’s sponsored insurance vehicles.&amp;nbsp; Reporting to the Head of Insurance Tax Structuring, this role will serve as a key technical resource for investment structuring, tax planning and ongoing tax support for KKR’s insurance platform, Global Atlantic.&amp;nbsp; This position requires deep expertise in investment structuring and international tax. This position would benefit from strong technical knowledge of insurance and reinsurance tax rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scope of the role is broad and dynamic, requiring excellent judgement in evaluating transaction structures, and the ability to collaborate effectively with internal stakeholders and external advisors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Investment Structuring &amp;amp; Transaction Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead tax structuring analysis for insurance company investments across asset classes, ensuring structures are optimized for the insurance company investors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on U.S. cross-border tax considerations, including withholding tax optimization, tax treaties, and foreign tax credit strategies and provide clear recommendations to investment deal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Deal Teams, Legal, Finance, and external advisors to structure new investments and resolve complex tax issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and oversee entity tax setup processes with external advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support due diligence and post-acquisition integration for insurance platform investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sponsored Vehicle Planning &amp;amp; Structuring&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide comprehensive tax planning and structuring support for KKR&#39;s sponsored insurance vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and implementation of new sponsored vehicle structures, including evaluation of domicile selection, entity classification elections (e.g., Section 953(d)), and investor considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ongoing tax planning and governance for existing sponsored vehicles, including monitoring for Permanent Establishment risk and BEAT risk and other US tax risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead tax analysis around exit options and restructurings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with external counsel and advisors on complex structuring matters, including rated feeder structures and other strategic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reinsurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on tax implications of reinsurance transactions and insurance structuring matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating Guidelines &amp;amp; Risk Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain operating guidelines to manage tax risks, including permanent establishment exposure and BEAT considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor insurance operations and investments to ensure compliance with operating guidelines, partner with legal and compliance team to provide advice to the business as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate periodic employee certifications and training, board training, and other governance activities related to operating guidelines compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategic Projects &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support broader strategic initiatives for the insurance platform as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on legislative and regulatory developments affecting insurance taxation and communicate impacts to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA, JD, LLM in Taxation or equivalent professional credential required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 7 years of relevant tax experience in a law firm, Big 4 accounting firm, insurance company, asset manager or financial services organization role, with strong experience in investment structuring and international tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in insurance/reinsurance is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and attention to detail, with the ability to assess complex tax issues and propose practical commercially grounded solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate across diverse teams and stakeholders and exercise sound judgement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment and meet tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
